\section{Encrypted Trait-Space Evolution Dynamics}
\label{sec:encrypted-evolution}

To preserve privacy and guarantee verifiable lineage continuity across
distributed compute nodes, the evolution of each computational organism is
performed entirely within an encrypted trait-space. Let the organism state be
defined as:

\begin{equation}
    O_i(t) = 
    \big(
        \mathbf{x}_i(t),\;
        \mathbf{g}_i(t),\;
        \mathcal{H}_i(t)
    \big),
\end{equation}

where $\mathbf{x}_i(t)$ is the continuous trait vector, $\mathbf{g}_i(t)$ is the
synthetic genomic sequence, and $\mathcal{H}_i(t)$ is the lineage-history tensor.
Under CKKS encryption, the trait vector is represented as a polynomial
ciphertext:

\begin{equation}
    \hat{\mathbf{x}}_i(t) = \text{Enc}_{\text{CKKS}}\big(\mathbf{x}_i(t)\big),
\end{equation}

allowing the evolution operator $\mathcal{F}_{\text{evo}}$ to be applied
homomorphically:

\begin{equation}
    \hat{\mathbf{x}}_i(t+1)
        = \mathcal{F}_{\text{evo}}^{\text{FHE}}
            \big(
                \hat{\mathbf{x}}_i(t),\;
                \hat{\mathbf{s}}_{\text{astro}}(t)
            \big),
\end{equation}

where $\hat{\mathbf{s}}_{\text{astro}}(t)$ is the encrypted astrophysical input
tensor derived from multi-messenger streams.

\section{Astrophysical Influence Operator}
\label{sec:astro-influence}

The influence of cosmic inputs on organism traits is modeled through a
multi-channel operator:

\begin{equation}
    \mathcal{F}_{\text{astro}} :
    \big(
        \mathbf{s}_{\text{Gaia}},\;
        \mathbf{s}_{\text{JWST}},\;
        \mathbf{s}_{\text{LIGO}}
    \big)
    \longrightarrow
    \Delta \mathbf{x}_i,
\end{equation}

where each component contributes distinct physical information:

\begin{align}
    \mathbf{s}_{\text{Gaia}} &\rightarrow 
        \text{kinematic drift, stellar density gradients}, \\
    \mathbf{s}_{\text{JWST}} &\rightarrow 
        \text{thermal flux, SED curvature, IR emission fields}, \\
    \mathbf{s}_{\text{LIGO}} &\rightarrow 
        \text{strain amplitude, merger chirp mass, ringdown modes}.
\end{align}

The combined influence is evaluated directly on encrypted tensors using CKKS
polynomial arithmetic, ensuring that no raw astrophysical data is exposed to
untrusted nodes.

\section{Species Boundary Verification via zk-SNARKs}
\label{sec:snark-boundaries}

To maintain zero-trust verifiability, each lineage update is accompanied by a
zero-knowledge proof. For a transition $O_i(t) \rightarrow O_i(t+1)$, the node
generates a Groth16 proof $\pi$ asserting:

\begin{enumerate}
    \item The encrypted trait update obeys the astrophysical influence operator:
    \begin{equation}
        \mathcal{F}_{\text{evo}}^{\text{FHE}}
        \big(
            \hat{\mathbf{x}}_i(t),\;
            \hat{\mathbf{s}}_{\text{astro}}(t)
        \big)
        = \hat{\mathbf{x}}_i(t+1).
    \end{equation}

    \item The coalescent divergence threshold was evaluated correctly:
    \begin{equation}
        d\big(O_a(t), O_b(t)\big)
        > \delta_{\text{speciation}}
        \;\Rightarrow\;
        \text{new species node}.
    \end{equation}

    \item The lineage-history tensor $\mathcal{H}_i(t)$ was updated without
          revealing internal trait-space values.
\end{enumerate}

Verification is performed using the public verification key $\text{vk}$:

\begin{equation}
    V\big(
        \text{vk},\;
        \text{Hash}(O_i(t)) \Vert \text{Hash}(O_i(t+1)),\;
        \pi
    \big) = 1.
\end{equation}

\section{OWL 2 Ontological Continuity Constraints}
\label{sec:ontology-continuity}

The ontology graph enforces semantic consistency across evolving species nodes.
Each organism is bound to its species class through the object property
\texttt{species:belongsToSpecies}. Continuity constraints ensure:

\begin{enumerate}
    \item Every organism has exactly one species assignment:
    \begin{equation}
        \texttt{FunctionalProperty}(\texttt{species:belongsToSpecies}).
    \end{equation}

    \item Species nodes inherit astrophysical provenance:
    \begin{equation}
        \texttt{species:derivesFromPhysicalPhenomenon}
        \subseteq
        \texttt{astro:AstrophysicalStream}.
    \end{equation}

    \item Lineage splits create new OWL individuals under
          \texttt{species:ComputationalSpecies}.
\end{enumerate}

These constraints allow the ontology to serve as a real-time semantic ledger of
cosmic-driven evolutionary dynamics.

\section{Distributed Execution and Privacy Guarantees}
\label{sec:distributed-execution}

The engine is designed for deployment across heterogeneous, potentially
untrusted compute environments. Privacy and correctness are maintained through:

\begin{itemize}
    \item Fully homomorphic evaluation of trait updates.
    \item Zero-knowledge verification of lineage transitions.
    \item Ontological consistency checks across distributed nodes.
    \item Encrypted multi-messenger astrophysics ingestion.
\end{itemize}

The execution stack integrates:

\begin{itemize}
    \item C++20/Rust SIMD kernels for high-throughput evolution.
    \item CUDA polynomial ring arithmetic for CKKS ciphertexts.
    \item Python ingestion pipelines for Gaia, JWST, and LIGO streams.
    \item OpenFHE/SEAL and arkworks-rs for cryptographic operations.
\end{itemize}

Together, these components form a unified, privacy-preserving evolutionary
simulation engine driven directly by real astrophysical phenomena.